  "id": "stuffit",
  "neon": "#d8c8a0",
  "note": "STUFF IT — the taxidermist on Kiln Lane, the first shopfront up from the South Gate.\n\nThe tile's prose: a stuffed hare on a green baize plinth behind canted glass, the sign painted\nblack on the cream render (STUFF IT, and under it MOUNTS · TANNING · SKULLS · NO PETS), and above\nthe sign something with a wingspan mounted on a bracket, weathering.\n\nSo the shopfront is a projecting bay window under a cornice, lit warm and green inside, with the\ndoor beside it. The name and the trade line are paint, not boards. The mount over the sign is a\ndark wing-shaped panel on a bracket standing off the wall. The cream render runs round all four\nsides with a plinth and a cornice; the upstairs has two sash windows.",
